From: ZedingZhang <me@zedingzhang.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Vulkan depth target format queries

Upstream google/filament PR #10424, for issue #10418, rebased onto the 1.75.0
tree this build links. Not yet merged upstream; carried here until it is.

VulkanDriver::isRenderTargetFormatSupported tested COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT, which
no depth or stencil format ever carries, so every one of them answered
"unsupported" however the device was built. The caller that picks a
depth/stencil format has no other way to ask, so it allocated
DEPTH32F_STENCIL8 regardless: on a device without it -- the Raspberry Pi 5's
V3D reports optimalTilingFeatures 0 for VK_FORMAT_D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT -- the
first attachment view over that image segfaults inside vkCreateImageView.

The query now asks for DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_BIT for depth and stencil
formats, and STENCIL8 joins the formats that are not mipmappable.

Harmless on a desktop GPU that supports DEPTH32F_STENCIL8, which is why the
parity probe never showed it; it is the Pi that crashes.
--- a/filament/backend/src/vulkan/VulkanDriver.cpp
+++ b/filament/backend/src/vulkan/VulkanDriver.cpp
@@ -1840,6 +1840,7 @@
 
 bool VulkanDriver::isTextureFormatMipmappable(TextureFormat format) {
     switch (format) {
+        case TextureFormat::STENCIL8:
         case TextureFormat::DEPTH16:
         case TextureFormat::DEPTH24:
         case TextureFormat::DEPTH32F:
@@ -1868,7 +1869,10 @@
     }
     VkFormatProperties info;
     vkGetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties(mPlatform->getPhysicalDevice(), vkformat, &info);
-    return (info.optimalTilingFeatures & VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT) != 0;
+    VkFormatFeatureFlags const requiredFeature = isDepthFormat(format) || isStencilFormat(format)
+            ? VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_DEPTH_STENCIL_ATTACHMENT_BIT
+            : VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_BIT;
+    return (info.optimalTilingFeatures & requiredFeature) != 0;
 }
 
 bool VulkanDriver::isFrameBufferFetchSupported() {
